  "description": "Mountain Bike Action, March 2007 - \"We've said, 'the Teocali is good news for the Mongoose faithful (and those new to the brand). For way less than $2500, you get a super-fun and super-capable trail bike. Riders who frequent rought and rocky trails will benefit the most from the FreeDrive rear suspension, but riders on smoother terrain don't have to pay a penalty in suspension bobbing or weight.' There are four models (one for women riders) from $1100 to $2300.\" Mountain Bike, November 2006 - Named BEST VALUE in Gear of the Year issue. \"The all-mountain wars continue to rage, with not only more travel coming each year, but also better-dialed travel at killer prices. Speaking of the latter, we're blown away by this amazing steal. The 31-pound Teocali Elite offers a great air-sprung suspension with nearly 6 inches of travel front and rear. Bonus points: a high-quality spec, even at this blue-collar sticker.\"",
